title: 'statement gossip: drive initial sync with a cursor over the admission journal'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The statement gossip initial sync snapshotted every statement hash per
    connecting peer (a full store scan and up to 2 MiB per peer) and could
    deliver a statement twice, through the snapshot and a propagation tick
    around it, costing duplicate-statement reputation penalties. The sync now
    walks the store's admission journal behind a per-peer cursor: scheduling
    captures the journal watermark in constant time, and the peer's propagation
    skips admissions below the watermark, so every statement reaches a peer
    through exactly one path.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `sp_statement_store::StatementStore` gains `admission_watermark` and
    `admitted_statements` (a filtered walk of the admission journal returning
    the new `AdmittedBatch`). `take_recent_statements` now returns
    `(u64, Hash, Statement)` triples carrying admission sequence numbers,
    oldest first. `statement_hashes` is removed.
crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
